"""
Chin Hin's Leadership Principle - 360 Review - multi-rater feedback on the 7 Leadership Principles.

Run:
    python build_db.py    # one-off, seeds leadership360.db from the old app's data
    python app.py         # http://127.0.0.1:5001

Model
-----
There is NO self-assessment and NO functional/technical competency. Every
person ("subject") is rated on the 7 leadership principles by a panel of
~5 assessors drawn from a mix of:

    line_manager   - the subject's own manager
    peer           - someone who shares the subject's manager
    direct_report  - someone who reports to the subject

Each (subject, assessor) pair is one row in `assignments`. The assessor
answers every behavioural statement at the SUBJECT's job grade with
Demonstrate (yes) / Developing (no). Per-assessor score uses the same
weighting as the original tool by default (Demonstrate 1.0 at the current level, 1.5 at the next, Developing 0), now a
setting per cycle (Points per answer: points_for(); a 1+1 framework's maximum is 35 at those defaults).

The subject's 360 result is the AVERAGE of the scores of assessors who have
submitted, mapped to a Low / Mid / High Potential band.

Visibility: only admin/HR sees results. A non-admin only ever sees their own
assessor queue and the rating forms for people assigned to them. Assessors
cannot see each other or any aggregate.
"""
